    {
      "id": "a117-q4",
      "type": "single",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "stem": "Why *greičiausias*, not *greitiausias*?",
      "options": [
        "Because *greitas* is irregular like *geras*.",
        "Because *-iausias* begins with a back vowel, before which *t* softens to *č*.",
        "Because superlatives never keep the stem consonant.",
        "Because it is feminine."
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explanation": "The same softening as in genitive plurals and past *-iau* forms. Sound rule, not a lexical quirk — except that *geriausias* uses a different stem from *geras*.",
